# A report waiting for its turn is dropped once the board no longer leaves the card out
# (#303's behaviour review, round 2, should-fix 1). Another program writes a board with a
# card left out while a duplicate's message shows, then gives the card an id before the
# message's time is up: nothing is reported. Written again with the card left out, it is.
size 160x44
env COLD_LAVA_EDITOR=none
wait-for example-workspace 35 notes
keys p
type krakatoa
wait-for 1 notes
keys enter
wait-for Volcanoes/Krakatoa  reading
keys D
wait-for duplicated as Krakatoa 1 · R rename
write Inbox/Tephra.canvas {"nodes":[{"id":"","type":"text","text":"- [ ] Sweep the roof","x":0,"y":0,"width":200,"height":80}],"edges":[]}\n
wait 1500ms
write Inbox/Tephra.canvas {"nodes":[{"id":"t","type":"text","text":"- [ ] Sweep the roof","x":0,"y":0,"width":200,"height":80}],"edges":[]}\n
wait-gone duplicated as
wait 1500ms
expect-not couldn't read
write Inbox/Tephra.canvas {"nodes":[{"id":"","type":"text","text":"- [ ] Sweep the roof","x":0,"y":0,"width":200,"height":80}],"edges":[]}\n
wait-for canvas couldn't read Inbox/Tephra.canvas: card 1 (id "") is left out
keys esc
wait-for ? help  q quit
keys q
exits 0
